[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'So, if you generate videos using MiniMax H3, you know about the main problem. The longer your video becomes, the slower the generation , and all this is due to the attention mechanism . Every frame interacts with every other frame, so the computational complexity grows quadratically.'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Double the length —and the work becomes much more than just double. But a new open-source project called Video Delta Net has emerged that solves this very problem. In this video, we\'ll see how it works compared to'

[00:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'other attention modes. So, here\'s the idea. Instead of each frame interacting with every other, Video Delta Net divides attention into two branches. Full attention is maintained for neighboring frames , so'

[00:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'local motion and sequence remain unchanged. And for the remote context, the model compresses it into a lightweight state that operates at a constant cost. Thus, attention changes from quadratic to'

[00:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'linear depending on the length of the video. The longer your video, the bigger the win. And the result is almost lossless quality. According to their benchmark, VDNA H3 renders a 14.4- second clip in about 11 seconds'

[01:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'on a cluster of 8 H200 GPUs. But we don\'t all have 8 H200 GPUs at hand, do we ? And here\'s the best part. Someone ported this to a native ComfyUI node format that runs on a single'

[01:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'consumer graphics card , and I ran it on my Pro 6000. On long clips, you get about a 2.6x speedup over the regular model with the same eight-step turbo sampling. It\'s also very easy to connect. You simply'

[01:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'put one node between the H3 loader and the sampler, load the branch weights—and you\'re done. No new base models, retraining, or additional Python packages. Let\'s take a look at this. So, both of the videos'

[01:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I\'m testing here use the quick video tuning that we talked about last time, and now VDNH3. And it is installed as a package of ComfyUI custom nodes. First of'

[01:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'all, you go into the manager, and after installation you get two things. Advanced model node with more options and a basic node. For this test, I am using an advanced VDN H3 node.'

[02:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'If you want to add it to your workflow, just search for the keyword VDN and these two nodes will appear. Essentially, it applies one patch node to the running kernel and then'

[02:14] [scene:talk]
